  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Philippines: Enhancing the Institutional Capacity of Prosecutors - Phase IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To support justice institution trainers to develop and implement training                programs for justice providers on priority topics related to criminal law. 2) To enhance partner justice                institutions&#x2019; tools, systems and processes to support Continuing Professional Development (CPD)                opportunities for target personnel. 3) To enable partner justice institutions to be prepared to                collaborate effectively on investigating and prosecuting priority crimes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Philippines Department of Justice 
(DOJ), National                Prosecution Service (NPS), Office of the Ombudsman (OMB), National Integrity Centre (NIC), Anti-Money                Laundering Council (AMLC), Philippines Judicial Academy (PHILJA), Legal Education Board (LEB). 
Indirect                beneficiaries: Persons involved in criminal cases, particularly related to money-laundering, businesses,                investors, students of law schools.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to enable partner justice institutions to perform core functions                in the criminal justice process in line with international standards and good practices.</narrative>
  </description>
